```

]
Two features of that table deserve attention before any comparison. First, `ORF1ab` and `ORF1a` overlap almost entirely: they are two products of the same stretch of sequence, because a ribosomal frameshift near position 13,468 lets the ribosome slip back one base and continue in a different frame. The GenBank location for `ORF1ab` is a #emph[join] of two intervals whose coordinates overlap by one base, which is how the format records exactly that event. Second, four of the genes are shorter than 100 codons, so no threshold-based ORF scan set at 100 will find them.

#block[
```
