GenBank, ENA and DDBJ form the International Nucleotide Sequence Database Collaboration (INSDC) \(Arita et al. 2020). They exchange new and updated records daily, so a sequence submitted to any one of them appears in all three within about 24 hours, under the same accession. The record content is the same; the presentation is not. GenBank shows you a flat file, ENA shows you an XML-or-flat-file service with a different browser, and DDBJ a third. A paper citing an ENA accession and a paper citing the same GenBank accession are citing the same data. Raw reads behave the same way: SRA, ENA and DDBJ's DRA mirror each other.

]
