body: 
[
The suffix after the full stop means different things in different resources, and all of them matter. In an INSDC or RefSeq nucleotide accession, the version increments whenever the #emph[sequence] changes --- `NC_045512.1` and `NC_045512.2` are different strings of bases. In a `GCA_`/`GCF_` assembly accession, the suffix versions the whole assembly, so new scaffolding alone will increment it. Ensembl versions genes and transcripts separately from the assembly (`ENST00000269305.9`), and increments the suffix when the model changes. An unversioned accession such as `NC_045512` silently resolves to whatever is current on the day you fetch it, which means an unversioned accession in a methods section does not specify the data you used. Always write the version.

]
