#strong[\6.] Two reasons it misleads: first, the fraction depends on how much attention a protein has received rather than on how well it is understood, so a heavily studied protein and an obscure one are not comparable; second, electronic annotations are added in bulk to every entry by pipelines, so an entry with few experimental annotations may simply have a large `IEA` denominator. It is informative within a single protein over time, or when comparing the same protein's entry between Swiss-Prot and TrEMBL, because then the denominator is controlled.

#strong[\7.] The block below is deliberately plain text so that it can be pasted anywhere.

#block[
```
from datetime import date

def provenance_block(row):
    """Format one manifest row as a four-line provenance record."""
    return (f"source:    {row['source']}\n"
            f"file:      {row['path']} ({int(row['bytes']):,} bytes)\n"
            f"sha256:    {row['sha256'][:16]}...\n"
            f"retrieved: as bundled; verified {date.today().isoformat()}")

print(provenance_block(entry))
