position: bottom, 
[
The choice of substitution matrix changes the alignment only when the sequences are distant. Each panel plots one quantity for three globin pairs aligned under five matrices with affine gaps (−11, −1): identity (left) and the number of aligned columns (right). The close and moderate pairs are flat lines --- every matrix recovers the same alignment --- whereas the distant haemoglobin-against-myoglobin comparison swings from 142 aligned columns under PAM250 to 101 under PAM30, with the apparent identity rising as the alignment collapses.
