Of 524 RefSeq coding sequences and 527 Prodigal predictions, 501 share a 3' end. That is roughly 95% gene-level agreement between an evidence-informed curated pipeline and a database-free #emph[ab initio] run, which is the usual state of affairs for a compact bacterial genome and should not be extrapolated to anything larger or more repetitive.

