Ramachandran plot of backbone dihedral angles for the p53 DNA-binding domain (1TUP chain B, blue) and sperm whale myoglobin (1MBN chain A, orange). Myoglobin occupies the α-helical region at lower left almost exclusively; p53 is concentrated in the broad β region at upper left. The empty areas are sterically forbidden, and a residue plotted there in a new structure is a modelling error until proved otherwise.
]), 
