Three views of the pasilla count matrix. Left: total mapped counts per sample differ by a factor of 2.6, so a raw count means something different in each column. Centre: the distribution of log2 counts per million is approximately symmetric once the log transform is applied, unlike the raw counts. Right: per-gene variance rises with the mean on logarithmic axes, the overdispersion that count-based models exist to handle.
]), 
