#> splice_acceptor_variant           103
```

]
Two facts stand out. Pathogenic and benign classifications are almost equally numerous, which is a property of #emph[TP53]'s intensive curation rather than of genes in general. And 956 records --- about a quarter of the file --- are variants of #strong[uncertain significance (VUS)]: the evidence is insufficient to classify them either way. The VUS is the central practical problem of clinical genomics, and its rate is far higher in genes and populations that have been studied less.

Review status records how much scrutiny a classification received, and ClinVar expresses it as a star rating.

