Variants that truncate the protein are classified pathogenic 81.4% of the time; missense variants only 16.9% of the time. This asymmetry is the ACMG evidence code PVS1 in empirical form: for a gene where loss of function is the disease mechanism, a truncating variant is strong evidence on its own, whereas a missense variant needs its specific effect established.

== Locating variants in a protein domain
<sec-13-domain>
ClinVar's VCF gives genomic coordinates, not protein positions. To ask whether pathogenic variants concentrate in a functional domain, each genomic position must be translated into a codon number, which needs the coding exon structure of the transcript. #emph[TP53] lies on the minus strand of chromosome 17, so codon numbering runs from high genomic coordinates to low.

The coding blocks of the MANE Select transcript ENST00000269305 were retrieved once from the Ensembl REST API \(Cunningham et al. 2021) and are written out below rather than fetched at build time, so that the book renders offline.

#block[
```
# Not executed at build time: the book must render without network access.
import json, urllib.request

url = ("https://rest.ensembl.org/lookup/id/ENST00000269305"
       "?expand=1;content-type=application/json")
transcript = json.load(urllib.request.urlopen(url))
translation = transcript["Translation"]
exons = sorted([(e["start"], e["end"]) for e in transcript["Exon"]], reverse=True)
blocks = [(max(s, translation["start"]), min(e, translation["end"]))
          for s, e in exons
          if max(s, translation["start"]) <= min(e, translation["end"])]
print(transcript["display_name"], transcript["strand"], transcript["assembly_name"])
print("CDS blocks (desc):", blocks)
print("total CDS nt:", sum(b - a + 1 for a, b in blocks))
```

]
