== Question bank: systems, data science and application
<sec-16-bank-11-15>
#strong[Chapter 11: Biological networks and pathway analysis]

#block[
#set enum(numbering: "1.", start: 47)
+ #emph[\(recall)] State what an edge in a STRING network asserts, and how that differs from an edge in a curated physical interaction database.
+ #emph[\(recall)] Define degree centrality and betweenness centrality, and state what each identifies.
+ #emph[\(application)] Given 80 genes from a differential expression analysis, describe how you would test for enrichment of a biological process, and state what the background universe must be.
+ #emph[\(interpretation)] In the bundled network #emph[TP53] has degree 29 of a possible 29 and five times the betweenness of the next gene, and degree correlates with Gene Ontology annotation count at Spearman 0.746. State the two separate reasons this hub status is not a discovery.
]

#strong[Chapter 12: Statistics and machine learning on omics data]

#block[
#set enum(numbering: "1.", start: 51)
+ #emph[\(recall)] State what the false discovery rate controls, and how it differs from the family-wise error rate.
+ #emph[\(application)] You will train a classifier on seven samples and 14,599 features. Describe a validation scheme that does not leak information, name the step most often performed incorrectly, and give the check that detects the leak.
+ #emph[\(interpretation)] Before normalisation the median log ratio between two untreated pasilla samples is 1.443; after conversion to counts per million it is 0.056. Explain what the first number is, and what would have happened to a differential expression analysis run on the raw counts.
+ #emph[\(interpretation)] A classifier on a test set with 2.4% positives has an ROC area of 0.858 but an average precision of 0.407 against a no-skill baseline of 0.024, with precision 0.706 and recall 0.308. State which summary is honest for this problem and what the model is actually doing.
]

#strong[Chapter 13: Bioinformatics in disease and healthcare]

#block[
#set enum(numbering: "1.", start: 55)
+ #emph[\(recall)] State what a variant of uncertain significance is, and why its existence is a statement about evidence rather than about the variant.
+ #emph[\(application)] A patient's exome contains a rare missense variant in a gene plausibly related to their phenotype. Give the steps you would take to assess it, in order, before any clinical statement is made.
+ #emph[\(interpretation)] In the bundled ClinVar slice, truncating #emph[TP53] variants are classified pathogenic 81.4% of the time against 16.9% of missense variants. Name the ACMG/AMP criterion this quantifies, and explain why the missense figure is not evidence that missense variants are usually benign.
+ #emph[\(interpretation)] 94.1% of pathogenic missense variants in #emph[TP53] fall in the DNA-binding domain, against 26.1% of benign ones and 48.6% expected from its length. State what this supports, which ACMG/AMP criterion it licenses, and what it does not tell you about any single variant.
]

#strong[Chapter 14: Working responsibly with genomic data]

#block[
#set enum(numbering: "1.", start: 59)
+ #emph[\(recall)] State why a genotype cannot be anonymised in the way a name can be removed, and give the quantitative basis for the claim.
+ #emph[\(recall)] Name the five dimensions of the five safes framework.
+ #emph[\(application)] You are asked to publish per-variant allele counts for cases and controls in a study of a stigmatised condition. State the attack this enables, the three inputs the attacker needs, and two modifications that preserve most of the scientific value.
+ #emph[\(interpretation)] A polygenic score validated in a European-ancestry cohort is proposed for clinical use in West Africa. State the mechanism by which its accuracy degrades, and what evidence would be required before deployment.
]

#strong[Chapter 15: A complete project, start to finish]

#block[
#set enum(numbering: "1.", start: 63)
+ #emph[\(recall)] State what belongs in a version-controlled repository for an analysis project and what must never be committed.
+ #emph[\(recall)] Explain what a Makefile records that a numbered list of scripts does not, and what `make clean && make` tests.
+ #emph[\(application)] Describe the test that establishes whether a project is reproducible, in the order the commands would be run.
+ #emph[\(interpretation)] Under genetic code 11 the capstone's first run recovered 96.6% of the 149 reference genes with no internal TGA but only 52.5% of the 375 that contain one. Explain why this single comparison identifies the fault, and name the two external checks that made the failure visible when the tool itself reported none.
]

#block[
#callout(
body: 
[
#strong[\47.] A STRING edge asserts a functional association supported by some combination of evidence channels --- co-expression, co-occurrence, text mining, databases, experiments --- combined into a confidence score. A curated physical interaction edge asserts that two proteins were observed to bind. In the bundled subnetwork every edge has text-mining support, 176 of 210 have experimental support and only 85 appear in a curated database, so treating the network as a map of physical contacts would overstate two-thirds of it.

#strong[\48.] Degree centrality is the number of edges at a node and identifies hubs. Betweenness centrality is the fraction of shortest paths passing through a node and identifies bottlenecks connecting otherwise separate parts of the network. A node can have high betweenness and modest degree, which is often the more interesting case.

#strong[\49.] Map the genes to the identifier space of the annotation source, test each term for over-representation with a hypergeometric test, and correct across terms with Benjamini--Hochberg. The background universe must be the set of genes the experiment could have detected --- the genes with non-zero counts in the assay, not the whole proteome --- because testing against an inflated universe credits you for the enrichment of expressed genes. The chapter's demonstration of this is blunt: matching the universe for study intensity cut the significant-term count from 511 to 121.

#strong[\50.] First, the network was built by querying a database for genes associated with p53 and the cell cycle, so #emph[TP53] is adjacent to every other node by construction; the topology reproduces the selection criterion. Second, degree in a literature-derived network partly measures how much a protein has been studied, which the Spearman correlation of 0.746 with annotation count makes explicit --- these genes carry a median of 54.5 Gene Ontology terms against a genome-wide median of nine.

#strong[\51.] The false discovery rate is the expected proportion of false positives among the tests declared significant; the family-wise error rate is the probability of making even one false positive anywhere. FDR is the appropriate choice when thousands of hypotheses are tested and a known, small proportion of false discoveries is tolerable, which is why it leaves 511 enriched terms where Bonferroni leaves 82.

#strong[\52.] Hold out a test set before anything else, or use nested cross-validation, with normalisation, feature selection and hyperparameter tuning performed inside each training fold only. The step most often performed incorrectly is feature selection on the whole dataset before splitting. The check is label permutation: with labels randomly shuffled there is nothing to learn, so a leaky pipeline that reports a mean accuracy of 1.000 in 100 of 100 permutations has been caught, while an honest one reports a value scattered around or below the majority-class baseline --- 0.384 against a baseline of 0.571 in the chapter's demonstration.

#strong[\53.] It is the log ratio of the two libraries' sizes showing up as an apparent expression difference: most genes do not change between two control samples, so the median log ratio measures sequencing depth rather than biology. Run on raw counts, a differential expression analysis would have called a large, systematic and entirely artefactual set of changes in the direction of the deeper library, and the effect would have been reproducible, which is what makes it dangerous.

#strong[\54.] The precision--recall summary is the honest one. With 2.4% positives the ROC area is flattered because the false positive rate is diluted by a large number of true negatives, so 0.858 sounds respectable while the model misses nearly 70% of the positives. What it is actually doing is being right when it commits --- precision 0.706 --- at the cost of committing rarely; whether that is useful depends entirely on the relative cost of a missed positive and a false alarm.

#strong[\55.] It is a variant for which the available evidence is insufficient to classify as pathogenic or benign. The classification describes the state of knowledge rather than a property of the variant, which is why reclassification is routine, why laboratories re-evaluate stored results, and why about a quarter of the #emph[TP53] records in ClinVar carry this label despite #emph[TP53] being among the most intensively studied genes in medicine.

#strong[\56.] Confirm the call itself --- depth, allele balance, mapping quality, and whether it lies in a region short reads resolve badly. Fix the transcript and the genome build, and express the variant in standard nomenclature against them. Check population frequency in a reference matched as closely as possible to the patient's ancestry, since a severe early-onset condition cannot be caused by a variant carried by 1% of people. Assemble consequence predictions, domain context and any functional data; consult ClinVar with attention to review status rather than label, and the literature. Then apply the ACMG/AMP criteria and consider segregation in the family. No clinical statement is made before confirmation in an accredited laboratory.

#strong[\57.] It quantifies PVS1, the criterion that assigns very strong evidence of pathogenicity to a null variant in a gene where loss of function is a known disease mechanism. The missense figure is not evidence that missense variants are usually benign: it is an average over a class that mixes the hotspot substitutions in the DNA-binding domain, which are almost all pathogenic, with substitutions elsewhere in the protein, which mostly are not. An average over a heterogeneous class tells you about the class, not about a variant in it.

#strong[\58.] It supports the claim that pathogenic missense variants in this gene concentrate in a specific structural region far beyond what its length would predict, which is the population-level evidence behind PM1 --- a variant in a mutational hotspot or a critical functional domain. It does not tell you that a particular variant inside the domain is pathogenic; location is one moderate piece of evidence among several, and 26.1% of benign variants also fall inside the same domain.

#strong[\59.] Because the genotype is itself the identifier, so there is no field to remove. The chapter's simulation makes the claim quantitative: every one of 10,000 simulated individuals is unique at 25 independent common markers, and the random match probability falls below one in eight billion at 30 markers. The governing concept is therefore controlled access rather than anonymisation.

#strong[\60.] Safe projects, safe people, safe settings, safe data and safe outputs.

#strong[\61.] It enables an allele-frequency membership attack. The attacker needs the published case-group frequencies, allele frequencies for a matched reference population, and the genotypes of the individual being tested; because the case group is defined by the condition, confirming membership discloses the diagnosis. Defensible modifications: publish only the variants that reach the paper's significance threshold rather than the genome-wide table, which removes most of the accumulating evidence; or place the full summary table behind the same controlled access as the individual data and cite the accession in the paper.

#strong[\62.] The score's weights were estimated for markers that tag unobserved causal variants through the linkage disequilibrium structure of the discovery population. Where that structure differs, the tags no longer track the causal variants and accuracy declines with genetic distance, so the score misclassifies risk differentially by ancestry. Deployment requires validation in a sufficiently powered cohort from the target population, reporting both discrimination and calibration, with weights re-estimated or at least re-calibrated locally.

#strong[\63.] Commit code, configuration, the environment specification, the workflow definition and documentation --- everything a stranger needs to regenerate the results. Never commit derived results and figures, large raw inputs that are already archived under an accession, credentials, or any data under controlled access; a Git history preserves deleted files in earlier commits, so `git rm` does not undo the disclosure.

#strong[\64.] It records dependencies rather than order: which inputs and which scripts each output depends on, from which the tool computes what is stale. Listing the script itself as a prerequisite means editing the analysis invalidates its outputs, which is the dependency most often forgotten. `make clean && make` tests whether every result in the project can in fact be regenerated from the raw data by the code in the repository.

#strong[\65.] Clone the repository into an empty directory; create the environment from the pinned specification; verify the raw data against the checksums recorded in the manifest; run `make clean && make`\; then compare the regenerated numbers and figures against those in the manuscript. A failure at any step means the project is not finished.

#strong[\66.] Because the comparison splits the reference genes by the one property the wrong parameter affects. Genetic code 11 reads TGA as a stop, so genes containing an internal TGA are fragmented and their true 3' ends lost, while genes without one are unaffected --- and the recovery rates, 96.6% against 52.5%, follow that split almost perfectly, which no general deficiency of the predictor would produce. The two external checks were the independent RefSeq annotation, which showed 995 predictions against 524 genes, and the coding sequence length distribution with the coding density, which showed fragmentation rather than over-prediction: a median of 336 bp against 856 bp and a density falling from 94.6% to 77.1%.

